comprehensive webhook platform 

Complete Webhook Platform Components
Backend (AWS Lambda + Kafka):

    Lambda - Schema Registration API - Manages webhook event schemas with validation
    Lambda - Subscription Admin API - Handles webhook subscriptions and API key management
    Lambda - Message Ingestor API - Receives events, validates against schemas, publishes to Kafka
    Lambda - Kafka Consumer & Delivery - Consumes from Kafka and delivers webhooks with retry logic
    Lambda - Delivery Status API - Provides delivery tracking, stats, and retry capabilities

Database:

    PostgreSQL Database Schema - Complete schema with tables, indexes, views, and sample data for:
        Webhook schemas
        Subscriptions
        Messages
        Deliveries
        Analytics
        Audit logs

Infrastructure:

    Serverless Framework Configuration - Full deployment config with API Gateway, Lambda, MSK integration
    Python Requirements - All necessary dependencies
    Docker Compose - Complete local development environment with PostgreSQL, Kafka, Kafka UI, pgAdmin

Frontend:

    React Admin UI - Beautiful, functional dashboard for:
        Managing subscriptions
        Registering schemas
        Viewing analytics and delivery stats
        Real-time monitoring

Documentation:

    Deployment Guide - Step-by-step AWS deployment with security, monitoring, and troubleshooting
    Local Development Guide - Complete local setup with testing examples

🚀 Key Features:

    Schema Validation: JSON schema-based payload validation
    Kafka Integration: Reliable message queuing with AWS MSK
    Retry Logic: Exponential backoff for failed deliveries
    HMAC Signatures: Secure webhook verification
    Analytics: Real-time delivery statistics and reporting
    Monitoring: CloudWatch integration and custom metrics
    Scalable: Auto-scaling Lambda with Kafka partitioning

💡 To Get Started:

    Set up local development with docker-compose up -d
    Deploy to AWS using the deployment guide
    Use the React UI to manage subscriptions and view analytics
    Monitor deliveries through the analytics dashboard

The platform follows the architecture with all the components:
API Gateway, Lambda functions, Kafka for queuing, PostgreSQL for storage, and webhook delivery with retry mechanisms!


